WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.834
-Hi, guys.

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:04.403
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.640
I hope everyone is staying at
home safe and healthy.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.642
Thank you so much
for watching our show.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.677
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.113
We have -- Chelsea Handler
is on the show tonight.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.748
-Did I draw that?
-Yep, you drew that.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:16.916
Thank you very much.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.152
Chelsea Handler,
who has one of the best lines

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.320
you'll hear later on tonight.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.488
She's like,
"I don't like FaceTime."

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.690
She goes,
"FaceTime is not for adults.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.691
The whole reason
I didn't have kids

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.660
is so I wouldn't
have to FaceTime."

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.228
Anyways, Chelsea Handler --

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.864
that's her charity
she's working with, Jersey.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.700
New Jersey is having
some tough times right now,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.902
so we're sending our thoughts
out to New Jersey.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.772
And we're going to get some help
for you guys tonight.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.008
Also, Kelly Clarkson.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.309
She hosts her own talk show.
She's doing it from home.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:45.778
She's on "The Voice."

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:50.116
And she has a new song out right
now in five different languages.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.952
Feedingamerica.org
is her charity.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.555
We love Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.623
And then we're closing out the
show with Michael McDonald,

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.192
who's going to do
one of his classics

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.260
and a song I think
fits perfectly

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.129
for quarantine time right now.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.164
Whyhungry.org is his charity.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.566
We love you, Michael McDonald.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.035
[ As McDonald ]
♪ We love you ♪

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.803
[ Normal voice ] We started
this yesterday, guys,

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:14.840
but our friends over at T-Mobile
really stepped it up.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.176
They're doing a thing with
Girls &amp; Boys Club

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:20.980
so that front-line and
healthcare workers

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.683
get some child-care
during this time right there.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:28.721
So if you text "thanks"
to 50555,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.925
it will be a $5 donation
going right into

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:37.564
Boys &amp; Girls Club for the
special COVID-19 Relief Fund.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.165
And T-Mobile said
they will match up to

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:43.402
$400,000 in donations,
so that is awesome.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.537
Thank you.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.872
And it could be any carrier,
by the way.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.173
Doesn't have to be T-Mobile.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.910
If you have whatever,
just text "thanks" to 50555,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.245
and it'll be great.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.548
Franny, are you cozy?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.916
-Are you cozy?

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.452
-I'm going to
put down my blanket.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:03.156
I'm going to go under --
-Do you have a blue tongue?

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:07.159
Let me see your tongue.
What is going on?

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.962
Where did you go?
-Dark, light.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.664
Dark, light.
-Dark and light.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.133
Okay, very good.
Long day of homeschooling.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.102
Let's do a monologue, everybody.
Here we go.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.437
♪♪
Okay, ready for the monologue?

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:21.007
Are you going to laugh?
-This is the...

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:24.677
-Oh, my God.
What is this character?

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:28.581
You don't smile like that.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:32.151
That's how you smile?
By not smiling?

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.687
Oh, my goodness. Alright.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.256
Oh, by the way, I will say,

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.057
Dude Perfect
is on the show tonight.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.225
We're going to do something
fun with those guys.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.859
We love Dude Perfect.
Thank you for that.

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:42.595
And before we do the monologue,

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.298
I just want to thank my wife,
who I love so much.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.899
I could not do any of this
without you.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.000
You're the greatest.
-I love you, too.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.401
-I love you so much.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:53.673
My wife, who's not
number one with technology.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.675
She's -- You know,
it's not on her list

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.009
of things that
she wants to get into.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:58.343
Anyways, she was trying
to help me out

00:02:58.343 --> 00:03:03.782
because we're doing a bit for
this giant relief concert

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:05.651
that's happening this Saturday.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.820
And, so, I wanted to see if
I can get an earpiece.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.456
And so Nancy thought maybe if
I painted the Air--

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:14.193
my AirPod brown that it would --

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.861
It would blend in with my ear,
thinking that

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:20.200
it goes up into my hair,
but AirPods go down.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.367
So she goes,
"Oh, that didn't work."

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.735
So then she painted it.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.504
She wanted to
paint it skin color.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:27.773
So these are my AirPods.
This is what they look like now.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:31.510
So no one can tell that
I'm wearing an AirPod.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.879
So thank you, honey.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.880
You were like --

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.249
Can you tell that I'm wearing
an earpiece, Winnie?

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:39.685
-Yeah.
-What?

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.421
-It's right there.
-Where?

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.090
-Yeah, thank you.
-Where is it?

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.091
-Where is it?

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:47.326
-Oh.
-No, I don't see it.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.028
♪♪

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.229
Alright, guys,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.097
welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:53.933
Well, guys,
this is very interesting.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.868
Satellite photos show
that the Earth

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:59.605
has been thriving since people
have had to stay inside.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.474
Damn, it's like we broke up
with Earth,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:05.077
and now it's coming back
with its revenge body.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.378
Some sports news.

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:09.781
The PGA Tour announced that
golf will return in June,

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:11.383
but without any fans.

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.052
I know I'll be watching,
mostly to hear

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.021
all the caddies sing
"Happy Birthday" twice

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:18.224
while using the ball washer.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.959
Of course, people who love to
gamble on sports

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.294
are also thrilled,
but they also were like,

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.696
"Hey, how much
you want to bet

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.700
it gets pushed back to July?"

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.202
So, today is
National Librarian Day.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:32.872
Man, between National Librarian
Day and golf coming back,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:39.178
this is a huge day for
people who love whispering.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.647
I read that Facebook
will start alerting users

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:45.051
if they've interacted with
coronavirus misinformation.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.986
Yeah, apparently, they send
you a message that says,

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:49.588
"You've signed into Facebook."

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:50.723
Listen to this.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.291
The C.E.O. of
the company that makes

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.026
"Call of Duty" and
"World of Warcraft"

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:57.463
gave out his personal phone
number to 10,000 employees

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.265
to help them
through the pandemic.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.900
When I heard that,
I was so inspired.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.768
That's why, today,
I gave all my employees

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:06.238
that C.E.O.'s phone number,
as well.

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.073
Experts are saying,
although it's difficult,

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:10.676
you should try to consume
healthy, mood-boosting foods

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.877
instead of comfort food.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.111
I'm trying my best.

00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:15.114
That's why for lunch,
I stuck a walnut inside

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.451
my tray of Totino's pizza rolls.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:21.287
You get the surprising nut roll.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.388
Some TV news.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.323
Earlier tonight,
ABC aired a special called

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.892
"The Disney Family Singalong."

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.794
Yeah. And this makes sense,
especially when it was

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:31.497
sponsored by Excedrin, Advil,
and Jack Daniel's.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:37.102
[ Laughs ]

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.472
I heard about a man in Michigan
who broke a record

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:42.241
for the most shots from behind
the backboard in one minute.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.509
And if you missed it,
don't worry --

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.979
ESPN will be airing it on a loop
for an entire week.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.380
And, finally,
I read about a couple

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:52.618
that named their baby Sanitizer
because of the pandemic.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.720
Yeah, in a few years,
he'll be in preschool with

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.957
Sourdough, Zoom Potato,
and Joe Exotic Jr.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:00.125
That is our monologue,
everybody.

